# `has-ansi` is committed here on purpose, and the repository root ignores every directory
# called `node_modules`, so this file un-ignores exactly this one.
#
# Why it exists at all: wrap-ansi 10's own suite opens with `import hasAnsi from 'has-ansi'`,
# and a vendored suite is run unedited — that is the whole contract. Without it the control
# run does not fail a case, it fails to *resolve*, and the host reads 0 / 1 with the reason
# buried in TAP diagnostics. Measured 2026-09-14, before this directory existed:
#
#     Error [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package 'has-ansi' imported from
#     packages/compat-oracle/vendor/wrap-ansi/test.js
#
# Why *here* rather than in the root manifest: a suite's own devDependency is not a
# dependency of this workspace, and putting it in the root manifest would put it in the
# lockfile, where it would read as one. `ansi-regex` is nested under `has-ansi` rather than
# left to the hoisted copy so this directory resolves on its own.
#
# A re-vendor used to delete this tree and this file: `vendor()` swaps a freshly built
# directory in whole, and #794's run dropped both. `hosts.ts` now lists them in this host's
# `keep`, which the vendor step carries across the swap, and `vendored-suite.test.ts` fails if
# a committed `node_modules/` path or root dotfile here is missing from that list.
!node_modules/

# ava's per-run scratch file. A record of which cases failed on this machine last time —
# never part of the suite, and it changes on every run.
node_modules/.cache/
